course: dictionary
lesson: 12911
title: Escort: going with someone to keep them safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Escort can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to escort someone means to go with them to protect them, guide them or keep them safe. «The teacher will escort the class across the busy road.» The clues are busy road and the teacher walking with the children, so escort means to go along and keep them safe.
explain: As a noun, an escort is the person, group or vehicle that does the escorting. «The king arrived at the castle with a police escort.» The police went along to guard him, so they were his escort.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simpler word. In «Two soldiers escorted the prisoner to the court», escorted could be replaced by guarded or taken along, and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you escort is about going with someone for protection.
fact: Escort can be a verb (to escort) or a noun (an escort).
fact: «Escort» means to go with someone to protect them, guide them or keep them under guard.
fact: An escort can be a person, a group or a vehicle, such as a car or a boat.
fact: «Under escort» means being taken somewhere with guards or helpers going along with you.
fact: «Escort someone home» means going with them so they arrive safely.
exercise: «The teacher will escort the class across the busy road.» What does escort mean here? | To lose them on purpose | To cook a meal for them | *To go with someone to keep them safe | To run away from them
exercise: «Two police cars were the escort for the famous singer.» What is the escort? | A ticket to the show | *A group that goes along to protect her | A song she sings on stage | A costume she wears
exercise: «Soldiers escorted the king through the town.» Find and copy the word that means went with him to protect him. | *escorted | town | through | soldiers
test: «Ella's dad will escort her home after the club.» Which phrase means the same as escort her home? | Leave her behind at the club | Race her to the house | *Go with her so she gets home safely | Send her a letter
test: «The gold was carried under escort to the bank.» What does under escort suggest? | *Guarded by people going along with it | Lost on the road | Hidden in a box | Sent by post
exam: In «A police escort led the bus to the stadium», what does escort mean? | A loud siren | A kind of bus ticket | *A group that goes along to guard the bus | A short journey
